+## ITM-01/02/04/05/20 experiment, Option A (restrained repair; docs/handoff/ITM_VISUAL_EXPERIMENT.md).
+## The original design deliberately hid empty trailing wells ("a trailing empty slot reads as broken,
+## what goes here?") and let the bar grow/shrink with the pack. This option bets that a QUIET empty
+## well -- an outline only, no fill -- reads as spare capacity rather than a defect, which is cheaper
+## than the geometry instability it removes: a bar that never resizes is easier to reach for by muscle
+## memory, and ITM-20 asks for exactly that. Nothing about the interaction model changes.
+const HOTBAR_WELL_A: Color = Color(0.20, 0.22, 0.28, 0.60)         ## lighter, semi-transparent (was UI_SLOT flat black)
+const HOTBAR_WELL_EMPTY_A: Color = Color(0.20, 0.22, 0.28, 0.16)   ## quiet capacity marker, no fill weight
+const HOTBAR_EDGE_QUIET_A: Color = Color(0.30, 0.34, 0.42, 0.40)   ## unselected border, quieter than UI_EDGE
+
+
 ## The carried pack as a hotbar of slots, icon and count, centred along the bottom. The active slot,
 ## which the mouse wheel cycles, is highlighted and it is the one the world verbs act with. It reads
 ## `sim.inventory_slots()`.
